  "I = I_s(e^(V/V_T) − 1), V_T = 25.9 mV at 300 K (n = 1).",
  "At 0.60 V: 1.0 mA.",
  "At 0.66 V: 1.0 × e^(0.06/0.0259) = 10.18 mA.",
  "Below about 0.5 V the current is too small to see on this scale: the familiar 'turn-on voltage'."
